   lock origin
   release operator origin
   mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready origin (no operator needed)
   allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate origin
   execute_origin_dispatch origin
   detach_task_profile origin

But note mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready requires transport_leg_assembled and transport_leg_loading_authorized, which we haven't done yet. So we cannot mark origin dispatch ready before assembling leg and authorizing loading. So we need to postpone origin dispatch steps until after transport leg assembled and loading authorized.

Thus we need to assemble leg and authorize loading before we can mark origin dispatch ready.

Thus we need to do origin lock, destination lock, assemble leg, authorize loading, then mark origin dispatch ready, allocate dispatch slot, execute origin dispatch.

Thus origin block must be split: we need origin locked before assembling leg, but we can't mark dispatch ready until after leg assembled and loading authorized.

Thus we can do origin prepare (attach, confirm, activate, assign operator, lock, release operator) then later after leg assembled and loading authorized, we do mark origin dispatch ready, allocate slot, execute.

Thus we need to keep origin_availability_locked and origin_availability_confirmed true after lock; they persist.

Thus we can do origin prepare early, keep lock, then later do mark dispatch ready etc.

Similarly destination lock needed before assemble leg.

Thus we can do origin prepare, destination prepare, assemble leg, authorize loading, then mark origin dispatch ready, allocate slot, execute origin dispatch, then later shift processing.

Now we need to ensure we have task profile available for each block as needed.

Let's design steps:

Phase A: Prepare origin (with task profile linked):
